{"id":"general-library_at_a_glance:e0012","type":"paragraph","page":1,"text":"Collection Development: We religiously follow the second and the third law when it comes to collection development. We go a step ahead when it comes to making available resources whether print or electronic by involving all the stake holders e.g, faculty members, students and researchers. It complements and supplements the scholarly and informational needs of faculty, students and researchers. Right from the day of inception it is aggressively building on its collection in varieties of forms like printed text books, reference books , magazines, newspapers and e resources like IEEE xplore, E-book collection of McGraw Hills etc. Digital Library section of the Central Library has developed an institutional digital repository using open source software DSpace, which preserve the institute's intellectual output for the posterity. Library has a separate section for books on history/flora & fauna of Chhattisgarh.","bbox":null,"level":null,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
